WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.920
Welcome to Grade 2 English, Unit 5: Let's Measure.

2
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:07.573
In this unit you learn to count
in tens all the way to one hundred.

3
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:13.480
You name the shapes circle, square, triangle,
rectangle and heart, and you spot patterns that repeat.

4
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:20.240
Best of all, you learn to measure and compare: which is
bigger, which is longer, which is taller and which is heavier.

5
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.940
You measure with a ruler in
centimetres and metres, ask “How many…?”

6
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:31.540
and answer with There is or There are, and you sort
out the number words that sound like other words.

7
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.940
Measuring carefully helps us understand
the world and be fair to everyone,

8
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:40.360
just like Amal and her friends in this
unit's story, “A Fair Way to Measure”.

9
00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:46.280
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.220
By the end of this unit, you will be able
to count in tens from ten to one hundred,

11
00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:55.720
and choose the right number word
when two words sound the same.

12
00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:01.080
You will also name and describe the shapes
circle, square, triangle, rectangle and heart.

13
00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.980
You will also notice, continue and
describe a pattern that repeats.

14
00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.720
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

15
00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:14.580
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: park, dark, card, start, number, add.

16
00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:19.700
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

17
00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:24.620
The reading sequence includes Shapes
All Around Us and A Counting Song.

18
00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:30.180
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

19
00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.440
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

20
00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:39.827
The first language focus is Comparing Two Things (-er than).

21
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:46.140
When we measure, we usually want to say which of
two things is bigger, longer, taller or heavier.

22
00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:52.690
To compare two things we add -er to the
describing word, and then we use the word than.

23
00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:56.520
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

24
00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:01.160
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 — Count in Tens.

25
00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.960
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

26
00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:11.520
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

27
00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:13.300
You are ready to begin.

28
00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:19.860
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

29
00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:26.140
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
